      "anchor": "p-real-sign-in-mail#field-4",
      "kind": "field",
      "label": "Real Sign-In Mail",
      "excerpt": "The service: Postmark, of Q12's two (Q12 A, a mail service) . Its whole business",
      "text": "Domains registered at SquareSoace",
      "by": "owenoak",
      "at": "2026-11-05T12:51:53.828Z",
      "status": "answered",
      "quote": "Find where each domain's DNS lives",
      "offset": 1921,
      "edited": "2026-11-05T12:52:00.185Z",
      "replies": [
        {
          "by": "owenoak",
          "agent": "claude",
          "at": "2026-11-05T12:58:50.860Z",
          "html": "<p>Done: the DNS steps are Squarespace's now, on their own page, <a href=\"/guides/atmosphere/mail-setup.html\" target=\"src-guides-atmosphere-mail-setup-html\">Setting Up Spell's Mail</a> (linked from the atmosphere guide).</p>\n<ul>\n  <li>Squarespace: the domain › DNS › DNS Settings › Custom Records › Add record. Delete any old MX record or email preset first; leave the website's \"Squarespace Defaults\" alone.</li>\n  <li>A table of the nine records each domain needs (Fastmail, Postmark, SPF, DMARC), and Squarespace's one-click Fastmail preset as a shortcut.</li>\n  <li>The other registrars' menus are gone; <code>dig NS</code> stays only as an optional check.</li>\n</ul>"
        }
      ],
      "claim": {
        "by": "owenoak",
        "agent": "claude",
        "at": "2026-11-05T12:58:50.268Z"
      }
    },
    "c2": {
      "anchor": "q17",
      "kind": "item",
      "label": "The host we buy for orgs: ask eny.space first, run Bluesky's host on a rented machine, or partner with Eurosky?",
      "excerpt": "The host we buy for orgs: ask eny.space first, run Bluesky's host on a rented machine, or partner with Eurosky?",
      "text": "New phases are too much for me to handle right now, let's start with \n- move up order for technical things you can do against alpha spaces at bluesky\n- doc linked to from this page for setting up postman, railyard, (squarespace? other?) for mail accounts and domains",
      "by": "owenoak",
      "at": "2026-11-05T13:00:01.649Z",
      "status": "answered",
      "replies": [
        {
          "by": "owenoak",
          "agent": "claude",
          "at": "2026-11-05T13:07:54.350Z",
          "html": "<p>Both done. The guide is <a href=\"/guides/atmosphere/mail-and-hosting.html\">Mail, Domains And Hosting</a>, linked at the top of this page.</p>\n<p>The phases now start with the technical work I can build and test myself, against Bluesky's Spaces alpha, with nothing from you:</p>\n<ol start=\"13\">\n  <li>P13 · A Spaces Host</li>\n  <li>P14 · Write Server And Proxy (its first step is now <a href=\"#t38\">T38</a>, the room-writes fix from <a href=\"#i8\">I8</a>)</li>\n  <li>P15 · Files In Spaces</li>\n  <li>P16 · Handles Under Spell (the DNS record waits for a real host)</li>\n  <li>P17 · Projections</li>\n</ol>\n<p>Then the ones that need you, or an answer:</p>\n<ul>\n  <li>P18 · Real Sign-In Mail: your Postmark and Fastmail accounts, and the domain records</li>\n  <li>P19 · Bluesky Sign-In: Q26</li>\n  <li>P20 · Org Roles: Q20, Q21, Q25; and after it P21 · Org Recovery, P23 · Writes By Role, P24 · Member Lists And Audits, P25 · Admin Page, P26 · Publish By Role</li>\n  <li>P22 · Paired Spaces: Q22, Q25</li>\n  <li>P27 onward wait on those, plus Q23 (inboxes), Q24 (email), Q17 and money for P35 · Setting Up An Org, and the stores for P37–P39</li>\n</ul>\n<p>None of the first five waits on an open question.</p>"
        }
      ],
      "claim": {
        "by": "owenoak",
